          "court": "Supreme Court of Oklahoma",
          "year": 2015,
          "date_decided": "2015-06-09",
          "holding": "Resolving a split among Court of Civil Appeals panels, the court reversed a termination judgment and held that due process requires the particular conditions a parent failed to correct be specified in the State's application, the jury instructions, the verdict forms and the final order.",
          "relevance": "Systemic instruction and pleading defects of the kind corrected here are exactly the judicial-determination quality issues federal reviews examine.",
          "quote": "Given the gravity of the rights implicated, vigilant enforcement of the full panoply of procedural safeguards must be carried out in child deprivation cases.",
